 ## Queue and Tickets
 
+### Queue
+
+A queue belongs to exactly one entity and owns every ticket issued into it.
+
+- `entity_id` — owning entity; queues are cascade-deleted with the entity.
+- `name` — display name.
+- `slug` — unique within the entity (`(entity_id, slug)`).
+- `is_active` — defaults to `true`; inactive queues reject new tickets.
+- `labels_i18n` — optional JSON labels per locale.
+
 ### Ticket
 
-Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
+Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `status`, `called_at`, `called_by_user_id` and `updated_at`. Attributes:
 
+- Display `code` — per-queue sequence `A001`, `A002`, ... (`A` prefix, at least three digits, zero padded; beyond `A999` it simply grows: `A1000`, `A1001`). Unique per `(queue_id, code)`.
 - Source queue — the ticket belongs to **one** queue (within the entity); does not record which totem it came from.
-- Priority (numeric, see below).
+- Priority (numeric integer, `>= 0`, higher = more prioritized; default `0`), see below.
 - Issuance timestamp (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
-- Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc.
+- Issuance channel: `totem`, `virtual` (default) or `printed`.
+- Status: `waiting` or `called` (there is no cancelled status).
+- Call fields: `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` (nullable FK to users), both empty until the ticket is called.
+
+### Issuance
+
+`App\Actions\IssueTicket` issues a ticket transactionally:
+
+- Rejects inactive queues with `InactiveQueueException`, reading and locking the queue row from the database inside the transaction so a stale active model cannot bypass a deactivation that happened after it was loaded.
+- Rejects a negative priority with `InvalidArgumentException`.
+- Creates a `waiting` ticket with `issued_at = now()`, channel `virtual` by default and priority `0` by default.
+- Computes the next display code from the last valid code by insertion order (malformed legacy codes are skipped) and retries a few times on a concurrent `(queue_id, code)` collision.
+
+### Write-once and calling
+
+After issuance every ticket field is immutable except `status`, `called_at` and `called_by_user_id`; any other Eloquent save/update throws `LogicException`.
+
+A ticket is called exactly once. `Ticket::call(User $user)`:
+
+- only accepts a `waiting` ticket (`LogicException` otherwise);
+- only accepts a member of the ticket's entity (`AuthorizationException` otherwise, ticket unchanged);
+- marks it `called` and records `called_at` and the calling user.
+
+Selecting *which* waiting ticket to call next (priority/fairness) remains a separate domain step.
+
 
